                {"heading": "Keep systems supported and updated", "body": "Operating systems and applications contain defects, and some can create security weaknesses. Vendors publish updates that fix known issues; attackers often study those updates to understand what unpatched systems may expose. Apply supported security updates through trusted management tools, prioritize internet-facing and critical systems, and plan for devices that can no longer receive fixes. An update process should include testing, ownership, and a way to confirm installation."},
                {"heading": "Use the least privilege", "body": "Least privilege means giving an account only the access it needs for its current task. Use a standard account for everyday activity and a separate administrative account for tasks that require it. This reduces accidental changes and limits what malicious software can do after a user-level compromise. Lock screens when stepping away, enable device encryption where appropriate, and remove accounts and software that are no longer needed."},
