                {"heading": "Three control purposes", "body": "Preventive controls aim to stop an unwanted event, such as access restrictions or secure configuration. Detective controls help identify activity, such as alerts and audit logs. Recovery controls help restore normal operation, such as tested backups and incident procedures. One control can serve more than one purpose. A strong program combines them so a missed prevention does not leave the organization blind or unable to recover."},
